## Code rules

- Follow the existing pattern. Before you design something new, find how the repo solves the same problem and match it. If you diverge, say why.
- Never hardcode a value that a contract, an enum, a config or an API response gives. Import it.
- After you fix a defect, search sibling code for the same defect, and fix it or report it.
- Doc comments on public functions, in ASD-STE100.
- Use the latest package versions: install them with the package manager, never type a version by hand.
- No secrets in code, config fallbacks or fixtures.

## Plans

- Plans live in `.plans/`, named `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-<kebab-slug>.md`. Finished plans move to `.plans/done/`.
- Validation reports live in `.plans/.validations/`. Run reports live in `.plans/auto-runs/` (gitignored).
- `@@PARENT_PLAN@@` is the parent plan. Child plans are written one step ahead.
- Every plan starts only after an explicit "go" from the owner. One plan per run.
- When a plan needs an owner decision, do not guess. Write the question down and continue with the steps that do not depend on it.

## Workflow

`/skill-1-plan <what>` (writes the plan, then validates it) → push the plan to `@@BASE_BRANCH@@` → launch it in the plans dashboard → review the draft PR → merge → `bash .claude/scripts/auto-pipeline.sh --cleanup <slug>`.

- `/skill-1-plan` asks the owner one decision at a time, saves `.plans/<file>.md`, then runs `/skill-auto-validate-plan`.
@@IF MOD_CODEX@@
- `/skill-auto-validate-plan` loops (max 4 rounds): the `plan-validator` agent and Codex (when `codex` is installed) each write a report in `.plans/.validations/`, the valid findings go into the plan, and each round leaves a `-round-<n>.md` decision log. `/skill-validate-plan` is one Claude round with no edits.
@@END@@
@@IFNOT MOD_CODEX@@
- `/skill-auto-validate-plan` loops (max 4 rounds): the `plan-validator` agent writes `.plans/.validations/<plan-basename>-validation-<n>.md`, the valid findings go into the plan, and each round leaves a `-round-<n>.md` decision log. `/skill-validate-plan` is one round with no edits.
@@END@@
- `/apply-validation` checks a pasted review (another agent, another session, a person) against the repo and writes `-external-<n>.md`.
- The dashboard runs `.claude/scripts/auto-pipeline.sh <mode> <plan>`. It creates a worktree `../worktrees/@@PROJECT_NAME@@/<slug>` on branch `auto/<slug>` from `origin/@@BASE_BRANCH@@` and runs `/skill-auto-pipeline` headless: `/skill-2-implement` → `/skill-3-test` → `/skill-4-verify` (`/code-review` loop + rule audit) → plan to `.plans/done/` and one commit for the whole plan → `/skill-5-ship` (draft PR). Modes: stop at verify (nothing committed), full (one local commit), to PR. The report is `.plans/auto-runs/<slug>.md`.
- `/skill-2-implement <plan file>` alone implements one plan in the current tree, with no commits.
- `/skill-3-test` and `/skill-4-verify` also run alone, after a manual `/skill-2-implement`.
- `/skill-5-ship` merges `@@BASE_BRANCH@@`, runs the checks, pushes the branch and opens a draft PR. Only when the owner asks.
@@IF MOD_TEST_REVIEW@@
- `/test-review` checks the tests of a change against the plan (the `test-reviewer` agent). The pipeline runs it after `/skill-3-test`.
@@END@@
@@IF MOD_CHANGELOG@@
- `/changelog-entry` writes the `changelog.d/` entry of a change. Every PR adds one, or carries the `no-changelog` label.
@@END@@
@@IF MOD_DECISION_SHEET@@
- `/decision-sheet` writes the decisions of a change for the reviewer. `/skill-5-ship` adds it to the PR.
@@END@@
@@IF MOD_PLANS_PARALLEL@@
- `/plans-parallel` reads `node .claude/scripts/plan-lanes.mjs --json` and proposes which plans can run at the same time.
@@END@@
@@IF MOD_PR_FEEDBACK@@
- `/pr-feedback <PR>` works the review comments of a PR in its run worktree.
@@END@@
- The skill names are a contract with the plans dashboard (it looks for `/skill-auto-pipeline <slug>.md` to see a live run, and copies `/skill-auto-validate-plan`). Do not rename them.
- Every skill runs shell commands bare: one command per call, no pipes, `&&`, redirection or heredocs. Headless runs auto-deny compound commands.

